    notes: 'Re-read 2026-10-05 against the actual printed-page scan images (p169-170, PDF 171-172 — not just OCR/transcription), now precisely separated from need.p169.fulfillmentH1Fortune, matter.p169.validityH6H8Planet, and need.p170.waterHousesRowOpen (the water-houses open/closed sub-rule, opened separately below with its own scan citation). Two distinct sub-notes remain genuinely unclosed: (1) "إذا سألك سائل: هل يصح ما سألت عنه أم لا؟ انظر إلى العاشر، فإن كان شكل داخل وهو في وتد، فإنه يكون قريب تحصيله؛ وإن كان فيما يلي الأوتاد، فهو يحصل بعد بطئ؛ وإن كان صاحبه في ساقط، فإنه لم ينل ما يطلب" (p169-170) — names "العاشر" (the Tenth) explicitly, then conditions on that SAME house also being "في وتد" (in an Awtad); since H10 is itself always one of the four Awtad houses (1,4,7,10) by the board\'s own structure (confirmed again directly from the p43 scan: "وفيها: أوتاد، ومواليات، وزايلات، وتسمى: ساقطات"), "وهو في وتد" would be a tautology if read as literally about H10 — genuinely ambiguous whether "العاشر" here means H10 specifically, a different counted position, or a secondary/derived figure not yet identified; not guessed past. (2) the FIRST of the two p170 water-houses notes, "هذا الشيء يحصل أم لا؟ كمل الضرب إلى السادس عشر، أقم من بيوت الماء شكلا، فإن حل ذلك الشكل في وتد أو بيت سعيد، وكان الشكل داخلا، فاحكم بتحصيل المسئلة" — WHICH houses "بيوت الماء" denotes is now closed (see need.p170.waterHousesRowOpen: houses 3/7/11/15, confirmed from the p43 and p47 scans), but HOW to "construct a figure from" four houses is not stated here or elsewhere in this source: it could mean stacking each house\'s own water row into a new 4-row figure, or successively combining the four houses\' full figures the way two figures are combined elsewhere in this book — the text does not say which, so this half stays blocked rather than guessing the procedure. Current v57 omits/shifts branches for both; no aggregate runtime is authorized for either. Do not infer a construction procedure for (2) from symmetry or another book.',
